{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception as a single automaton, capturing the interaction between motion commands and obstacle sensor events. The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and conservative turn recovery is triggered by obstacles. Recovery states only allow directed turns, and full_rotate is reserved for rare, deliberate scans. All uncontrollables are handled deterministically, and the design avoids oscillation and infinite controllable loops.",
  "strategy": [
    "Combine motion and perception into a single plant automaton to reflect the runtime coupling of actions and sensor outcomes.",
    "Specification enforces: (1) random_walk as the main exploration action in clear, (2) move_forward as a short progress step, (3) rotate_clockwise for obs_front and obs_left, (4) rotate_counterclockwise for obs_right, (5) full_rotate only as a deliberate scan, and (6) rapid return to exploration after recovery."
  ],
